  "transcript": "User: Hi — I saw your ad on Facebook about answering missed calls. I keep losing patients after hours, so I'm curious how it works.\nAgent: Got it — glad the ad found you. After-hours, when calls come in and no one picks up, do they usually leave a voicemail, or do they just call the next practice?\nUser: They often hit voicemail, but I'm worried they'll call a competitor if we don't answer.\nAgent: Yeah, that makes sense — after hours people usually want an answer fast. When those voicemails come in, do you have anyone calling them back that night, or is it usually the next day?\nUser: It's usually the next day, but I believe immediate response would secure more bookings.\nAgent: Right — next day is often too late for someone who’s anxious and just wants to get seen. Has anyone ever showed you the math on what those after-hours missed calls are costing you?\nUser: Not exactly, but I estimate about 20 calls a week, and half might book at $650 each.\nAgent: Got it — if you booked even 50% of those 20 missed calls, that’s about **$6500 extra a week**… and that’s roughly **$28100/mo** over a month. Does that feel about right?\nUser: Yes, that sounds about right. That's why I'm interested in catching those after-hours calls.\nAgent: Makes sense — that’s exactly where we help: we answer those after-hours calls, capture the details, and get them booked so they don’t drift to a competitor. It’s a 20-minute walkthrough with Jay so you can see how it works on your exact call flow—what’s better for you, later today or tomorrow?\nUser: I’d prefer tomorrow. Can we book the live call slot directly?\nAgent: Yes — we can book it. What’s your first name?\nUser: My name is Maria Gonzales. Let's go ahead and book the live call for tomorrow.\nAgent: Got it, Maria Gonzales — what’s the name of your practice?\nUser: It's called Bright Smile Dental.\nAgent: Perfect — and is the number you’re calling from the best contact number to reach you for the SMS confirmation?\nUser: Yes, my best contact is +13125551234. Please use this number for the SMS confirmation.\nAgent: Perfect — and which time zone are you in: Eastern, Central, Mountain, or Pacific?\nUser: I'm in the Central time zone, America/Chicago.\nAgent: Got it — Central time. Perfect. So I have Maria Gonzales with Bright Smile Dental, a contact number on file, and Central time — is that all correct?\nUser: Yes, that's all correct. Can we proceed with booking the live call for tomorrow?\nAgent: One moment while I check availability… okay—tomorrow I can get you in as soon as **10:00 AM** or **10:45 AM** Central time; which works?\nUser: 10:45 AM Central time works. Yes, book it.\nAgent: One moment while I confirm that.\nAgent: Thanks, Maria — you’re booked for **tomorrow at 10:45 AM Central** with Jay, and you’ll receive an SMS text with the confirmation details so you can add it to your calendar (or reschedule if needed). Is there anything else I can help you with?\nUser: Sure, I'll wait. Please let me know once it's confirmed.\nAgent: All set, Maria — it’s confirmed for tomorrow at 10:45 AM Central, and your SMS confirmation is on the way. Really glad you called—Jay’s looking forward to it. Have a great day. Bye!",
